{"term":"pause","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cd4c387549ecdc3b70","definition":"To take a temporary rest, take a break for a short period after an effort.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["nonpausing","pausable","pausingly","prepause","unpause"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pause#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3d60a52ab37d3d56a1","definition":"To stop (an activity) for a while.","example":"The general public could therefore have been forgiven for thinking that work on the new station had stopped. But pausing work on an active construction site of this size is not straightforward.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["nonpausing","pausable","pausingly","prepause","unpause"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pause#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d5c7533a9750486d1b","definition":"To interrupt an activity and wait.","example":"When telling the scary story, he paused for effect.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["nonpausing","pausable","pausingly","prepause","unpause"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pause#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:14588dea304ee60326","definition":"To hesitate; to hold back; to delay.","example":"Why doth the Jew pause? Take thy forfeiture.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["nonpausing","pausable","pausingly","prepause","unpause"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attrib